Root cause: NOT Git::Libgit2 and NOT the repository. karr called into libgit2 during Perl's global destruction. SyncGuard::DESTROY runs $git->push; on the CLI die path bin/karr catches the die and exits without releasing the guard, so the guard is first reaped in global destruction, where FFI::CheckLib's and FFI::Platypus's package globals are already freed. Git::Libgit2::FFI::ffi() then rebuilds from scratch and TypeParser::Version1::parse recurses without bound (~700 MB/s). Reproduces on Git::Libgit2 0.005 and on a brand-new empty repo, so neither the version nor repo size was ever the variable — only 'does the repo have a remote' (without one, push short-circuits before any FFI work, which is why the throwaway board in the ticket looked clean).

